 System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.5597) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-14900HX (32 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThere are two primary ways to create new files in Godot:\n\n1) Right click on a folder/file in the file system dock, and use the 'Create New' submenu:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3257cc57-8c5f-4e51-a059-5893593bc12c)\n\n2) Click directly on the backdrop of the file system dock, and you get an immediate contextual menu with 'Create...' options.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e0b3840c-1a00-45b2-9757-e904a2321d65)\n\n---\n\nThe `ContextMenuSlot::CONTEXT_SLOT_FILESYSTEM_CREATE` only adds a member into the *first* slot. The second slot doesn't appear to be data driven at all. I would like to see these two menus \"linked\" so that changes to one effects changes to the other. \n\nNote: One difference between these two menus is the inclusion of the 'New' keyword in the second one. I recall some discussion about this exact topic, actually, but I cannot find the issue. \n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOpen the MRP. You may need to enable the 'Create Actor' plugin. Attempt to create an actor using both workflows shown above. Only the 'Create New' menu shows the new 'Create Actor' option. \n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[create_actor.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20012188/create_actor.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_